import json, urllib.request
API='http://192.168.1.206:3100'
tickets=[
 {
  "title":"Lock the alias full-width contract across the whole render path",
  "goal":("PROBLEM: The alias screen was squeezed by a width cap (max-w-2xl, then a plan-guessed max-w-4xl = 896px on a 1440px page) while the issue explicitly complained the rest of the page sat empty. Both the implementation agent and the PR-review agent accepted the still-capped version; only a human rejection (\"make the most of the full width\") forced a full rework loop (design-note update, uncapped w-full min-w-0 section root, new desktop+mobile screenshots, test updates, re-review). The width target was a guessed Tailwind step, never a measurable criterion derived from the complaint. The current regression test (frontend/src/components/settings/SettingsCards.overflow.test.jsx, \"spans the full width\") locks only the section root and row classes, not the ancestor chain: App.jsx main -> settings section -> tabpanel -> ProjectSettingsForm wrapper -> alias section. A cap reintroduced on any ancestor (e.g. the max-w-2xl in ProjectSettings.jsx:259, today confined to the project-tab conditional) would re-squeeze the Aliases tab with no test failing. "
  "FIX: (1) Extend the overflow contract test to render the settings page on the Aliases tab and assert no max-w-* class (other than max-w-full/max-w-none) on the alias section or any ancestor between the settings panel and the section, so refactors cannot silently reintroduce a cap. (2) Add a one-paragraph rule where Plan agents will see it (frontend agent/UI guidance): when an issue complains about wasted space or truncation, the plan must state a measurable width criterion (uncapped w-full min-w-0 with no max-w on the render path; zero clipped elements at the stated viewports) instead of guessing a Tailwind max-w step, and must verify it headlessly. "
  "Case study with full history: task 158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972 (docs/tasks/158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972/: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Step 2, DESIGN-NOTE.md section (d), review-alias-redo-20261120.md, review-fullwidth-20261120.md, final-review-20261120-211044.md)."),
  "stageId":"1","workflowId":"wf-default","projectId":"0fd41821-d8a5-4e49-bc2e-28ce8c739a0a",
  "idempotencyKey":"c8b31f61b51bbb4f97d0ddda762c3809","execute":False,
 },
 {
  "title":"Add canonical model-ref test fixtures so invented refs cannot silently pass",
  "goal":("PROBLEM: Model references have a subtle grammar (shared/modelKeys.js: bare id, legacy provider::id, canonical harness::provider::id, and harness::provider::id::level; splitReasoning returns a reasoning level ONLY for 4-segment refs, so a 3-segment ref like google::m1::high parses as harness/provider/id with NO reasoning). An agent writing the AliasTargetChip reasoning-suffix test invented the 3-segment form expecting a ::high suffix; the test passed for the wrong reason (via the chip's sr-only full ref, not the muted-suffix span) and the silently-wrong coverage survived until a reviewer spotted it, costing a second fix-and-re-review commit. There is no canonical fixture module for model refs, so every agent invents refs from memory and can fall into the same trap. "
  "FIX: Add a canonical model-ref fixture module (follow the existing shared/toolLogFormat.fixtures.js pattern) exporting named valid refs for each grammar form plus documented INVALID traps (3-segment ::suffix is not reasoning; 5+ segments malformed), with a JSDoc table of form -> example -> parse result; link it from splitReasoning/parseModelKey JSDoc; migrate the alias chip/summary tests onto the fixtures; add one negative test asserting the 3-segment trap yields reasoning null. "
  "Case study: task 158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972 (docs/tasks/158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972/review-alias-redo-20261120.md non-blocking nit; fixed in the full-width follow-up per review-fullwidth-20261120.md)."),
  "stageId":"1","workflowId":"wf-default","projectId":"0fd41821-d8a5-4e49-bc2e-28ce8c739a0a",
  "idempotencyKey":"20eb1b22cde02cb8dd58e6068d8bf02c","execute":False,
 },
 {
  "title":"Provide a reusable fixture-driven component clipping harness for visual proof",
  "goal":("PROBLEM: Layout fixes need headless proof that no text is clipped (jsdom cannot measure layout), but the repo offers only whole-app capture (scripts/capture-screenshot.mjs needs a running app URL) and one-off inline snippets (a page-level scrollWidth check in canary-e2e/tests/mobile-responsive.spec.js; a jsdom width assertion in LogViewer.test.jsx). There is no reusable way to render one component with fixture props plus repo tailwind at stated widths, assert scrollWidth <= clientWidth per selector, and emit PNG proof to the task docs folder. On the alias redo the implementation agent skipped the required Step 6 screenshots entirely, and the reviewer had to hand-roll a scratch vite server on 127.0.0.1:4173 with fixture data to measure per-chip clipping - the exact ad-hoc-background-server pattern stage guidance forbids. Skipped proof plus hand-rolled harnesses doubles review effort on every visual task. "
  "FIX: Add a reusable headless component clipping harness (script + doc): renders a target component with JSON fixture props and repo tailwind at given widths (e.g. 1440 and 390), fails on any clipped target selector (scrollWidth vs clientWidth) and on page horizontal overflow, writes PNG captures defaulting to docs/tasks/<task-id>/ with PNG-magic self-verification following capture-screenshot.mjs conventions, and never requires a long-lived server. Document it in the Testing & Verification guidance; acceptance is reproducing the alias desktop+mobile no-clipping proof with one command per width. "
  "Case study: task 158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972 (docs/tasks/158394ab-3b43-4813-b94a-32d772a79972/: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Step 6, review-alias-redo-20261120.md visual-evidence section)."),
  "stageId":"1","workflowId":"wf-default","projectId":"0fd41821-d8a5-4e49-bc2e-28ce8c739a0a",
  "idempotencyKey":"b25b2d3bba81defabdf4720dd0103405","execute":False,
 },
]
for t in tickets:
    req=urllib.request.Request(API+'/tasks', data=json.dumps(t).encode(), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json'}, method='POST')
    try:
        resp=urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20)
        body=json.loads(resp.read().decode())
        print(resp.status, body.get('id'), '|', body.get('status'), '|', body.get('currentStageId'), '|', t['title'][:60])
    except Exception as e:
        import urllib.error
        if isinstance(e, urllib.error.HTTPError):
            print('HTTP', e.code, e.read().decode()[:500])
        else:
            print('ERR', repr(e))
EOF","description":"Create three improvement tickets via API"}

